{"description": "Adventures of Huckleberry Finn or as it is known in more recent editions, The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn, is a novel by American author Mark Twain, which was first published in the United Kingdom in December 1884 and in the United States in February 1885.\r\n\r\nCommonly named among the Great American Novels, the work is among the first in major American literature to be written throughout in vernacular English, characterized by local color regionalism. It is told in the first person by Huckleberry \"Huck\" Finn, the narrator of two other Twain novels (Tom Sawyer Abroad and Tom Sawyer, Detective) and a friend of Tom Sawyer. It is a direct sequel to The Adventures of Tom Sawyer.", "links": [{"title": "Adventures of Huckleberry Finn - Wikipedia", "url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventures_of_Huckleberry_Finn", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn (americanliterature.com)", "url": "https://americanliterature.com/author/mark-twain/book/the-adventures-of-huckleberry-finn/summary", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "Twain publishes The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn - february 18, 1885 - HISTORY.com", "url": "https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/twain-publishes-the-adventures-of-huckleberry-finn", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn book review (commonsensemedia.org)", "url": "https://www.commonsensemedia.org/book-reviews/the-adventures-of-huckleberry-finn", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "Amazon", "url": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/1543619665/ref=olp-opf-redir?aod=1&tag=wwwcampusboocom587-20&condition=new", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}], "title": "Adventures of Huckleberry Finn", "covers": [8157718, -1, 12242593, 12507992], "subject_places": ["Mississippi River", "Missouri", "Arkansas"], "subjects": ["Adventure stories", "American fiction (fictional works by one author)", "American literature", "Boys", "Child and youth fiction", "Childre